 "gotchas": [
  "All 6 joints are type=continuous: the SolidWorks exporter emitted NO joint limits (limits_deg=null). Real FAZE4 travel ranges must come from mechanical stops/docs, not this URDF.",
  "Mesh <mesh> tags have no scale attribute (scale=1,1,1) and vertex data is in METERS, not mm. three.js/most STL loaders will read raw values; multiply by 1000 only if the viewer works in mm.",
  "Link frames are NOT at part centroids or joint axes: visual origins are all identity, so each mesh is positioned in its link frame exactly as exported from SolidWorks (offset, arbitrary orientation). E.g. base_link mesh occupies x[-10,160] y[-300,-40] z[20,140] mm.",
  "Zero pose is NOT a home/upright pose: joint rpy values bake in arbitrary SolidWorks assembly angles (e.g. J2 yaw -103.77 deg, J3 yaw -67.34 deg), so at q=0 the arm appears in the bent pose it was assembled in CAD.",
  "J4 (podlaktica) axis is NOT axis-aligned in its child frame: axis=(0.14804, 0.90477, 0.39934) (unit vector). Its world direction at zero pose is what matters for articulation.",
  "Joint names equal their child link names (rotary_base, nadlaktica, ...), which can confuse name-keyed lookups.",
  "URDF rpy is fixed-axis XYZ (R = Rz(yaw)*Ry(pitch)*Rx(roll)).",
  "Croatian link names: nadlaktica=upper arm, lakat=elbow, podlaktica=forearm, saka=wrist/hand, hvataljka=gripper."
 ]
